; CPF merge for mirror member B of stack 3 - the instance that joins the mirror as
; the second failover member, and therefore starts as the backup.
;
; The same database and namespace are created here as on member A, both empty. The
; backup then adds its copy to the mirror and catches up from the primary. Because
; both copies are empty at that point there is nothing to restore, which is what
; makes this exercise quick - a real mirror is normally seeded from a backup of the
; primary.
;
; Deliberately NOT prepared - this is the exercise:
;   - %Service_Mirror is left disabled
;   - this member has not joined any mirror

[Actions]
ModifyUser:Name=SuperUser,ChangePassword=0

CreateDatabase:Name=MIRRORDATA,Directory=/usr/irissys/mgr/mirrordata

CreateNamespace:Name=MIRRORNS,Globals=MIRRORDATA,Routines=MIRRORDATA
